{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HQojoX6Djb7gPMRokMJKCX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verifying behavioral parity via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture**: SRDs (specs) feed an AI code generation pipeline. Each utility lives in `cmd/<name>/` with `main.go` + `<name>_test.go`. Shared infrastructure in `pkg/testutils` (diff testing), `pkg/sys` (syscalls), `pkg/format` (output), `pkg/hashutil`, `pkg/sizeparse`, `pkg/encutil`. Differential tests compare Go binary output against g-prefixed GNU binaries.\n\n**Implementation state**: Many releases are fully implemented (01.2, 01.3, 02.0, 02.1, 02.2, 03.0, 05.3). The earliest release with \"ready\" requirements in `requirement_states` is **rel08.1** — `fmt` has 7 remaining ready requirements (R10.1, R11.1, R12.1, R13.1-R13.4); `numfmt`, `od`, and `printf` are not started (16 ready requirements each).\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe earliest incomplete release with ready requirements is **rel08.1**. Within it:\n1. **srd070-fmt** — partially implemented, 7 requirements ready. Complete this first.\n2. **srd071-numfmt** — not started, 16 requirements ready. Start this next.\n3. srd072-od and srd073-printf queued after numfmt.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming weight 1 per requirement (default; cannot read requirements.yaml per constraints):\n\n- Task 0: srd070 R10.1(1) + R11.1(1) + R12.1(1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: srd070 R13.1(1) + R13.2(1) + R13.3(1) + R13.4(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: srd071 R1.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) + R1.4(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: srd071 R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) + R2.3(1) + R2.4(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/fmt: srd070 R10.1, R11.1, R12.1\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml (requirements R10.1, R11.1, R12.1 -- read the full SRD for context)\n      - cmd/fmt/main.go (existing implementation to extend)\n      - cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go (existing differential tests to extend)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- understand DiffTest and RunDiffTests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/fmt/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd070 requirements R10.1, R11.1, R12.1\n      - path: cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases covering R10.1, R11.1, R12.1\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd070 requirement R10.1 in cmd/fmt per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd070 requirement R11.1 in cmd/fmt per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd070 requirement R12.1 in cmd/fmt per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing cmd/fmt implementation -- do not rewrite or restructure existing code. Add only the logic needed for R10.1, R11.1, R12.1.\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern with pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests comparing against the gfmt reference binary. All test cases set LC_ALL=C.\n      - id: D3\n        text: Skip differential tests if the reference binary gfmt is not found via exec.LookPath (t.Skip pattern).\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: srd070 R10.1 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n      - id: AC2\n        text: srd070 R11.1 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n      - id: AC3\n        text: srd070 R12.1 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n      - id: AC4\n        text: go build ./cmd/fmt/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC5\n        text: go vet ./cmd/fmt/ reports no issues\n      - id: AC6\n        text: go test ./cmd/fmt/... -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if gfmt reference binary is not installed)\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/fmt: srd070 R13.1-R13.4\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml (requirements R13.1, R13.2, R13.3, R13.4 -- read the full SRD for context)\n      - cmd/fmt/main.go (existing implementation to extend -- includes changes from prior task)\n      - cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go (existing differential tests to extend)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- understand DiffTest and RunDiffTests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/fmt/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd070 requirements R13.1, R13.2, R13.3, R13.4\n      - path: cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases covering R13.1, R13.2, R13.3, R13.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd070 requirement R13.1 in cmd/fmt per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd070 requirement R13.2 in cmd/fmt per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd070 requirement R13.3 in cmd/fmt per the SRD specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd070 requirement R13.4 in cmd/fmt per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing cmd/fmt implementation -- do not rewrite or restructure existing code. Add only the logic needed for R13.1 through R13.4.\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern with pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests comparing against the gfmt reference binary. All test cases set LC_ALL=C.\n      - id: D3\n        text: Skip differential tests if the reference binary gfmt is not found via exec.LookPath (t.Skip pattern).\n\n    acceptance_cri